---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & Local Image Processing"
  description="What stays on your device, how saved settings work, and what ordinary website requests involve."
  noindex
  activeNav="/privacy/"
  ><header class="legal-hero legal-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">DAMA IMAGE PREP</p><h1>
      Privacy & Local Image Processing
    </h1>
  </header><section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <p>Updated September 7, 2026.</p><h2>Your selected image files</h2><p>
      The image workspace processes selected files in your browser. It does not
      upload them to Dama or store them in a server-side image library. Exports
      are created locally, and originals are not modified. There is no account
      or cloud synchronization.
    </p><h2>Saved settings</h2><p>
      Saving is optional. Width, height, fit, margin, crop position, background,
      format, quality, enlargement choice, sequence start and filename prefix
      are stored in this browser’s local storage. Photos and source filenames
      are not stored there. The prefix you enter is part of the saved settings.
    </p><p>
      Use “Forget saved settings” to remove the saved recipe. “Reset” changes
      the current controls but does not delete saved settings; “Clear batch”
      removes the active photos and results from the workspace. Browser
      site-data controls can also remove local storage.
    </p><h2>Ordinary website requests</h2><p>
      Loading the site involves network requests. Cloudflare, our hosting
      provider, may process connection and security information such as IP
      addresses, requested URLs and request times. Local image processing does
      not mean every website visit is anonymous. See <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a
      >.
    </p><h2>Advertising and analytics</h2><p>
      This release does not load advertising or analytics scripts. The
      publisher-verification meta tag and ads.txt record are identifiers, not
      advertising JavaScript. If advertising or analytics is enabled later, this
      policy and any applicable consent controls must be updated before those
      scripts run.
    </p><h2>Device caches and downloads</h2><p>
      Browser and operating-system caches are outside Dama’s direct control.
      Closing a tab is not a guarantee of secure erasure of all local traces.
      Downloaded files remain wherever you choose to save them. Follow your
      device’s privacy practices when using shared computers.
    </p><h2>External links and contact</h2><p>
      Links to marketplace documentation and GitHub open services with their own
      privacy practices. GitHub issue reports are public; do not post images,
      personal details or confidential business information. <a href="/contact/"
        >Contact and corrections</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section></BaseLayout
>
